  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "F1",
      "finding": "No host clock drift",
      "evidence": "Windows (China Standard Time, UTC+8, no DST, NTP time.windows.com), Python datetime/strftime, git var GIT_COMMITTER_IDENT and the platform-injected session clock all agree on 2026-11-08 ~17:43 +0800."
    },
    {
      "id": "F2",
      "finding": "Git timestamps are authentic and self-consistent",
      "evidence": "Raw commit objects carry epoch 1794130093 +0800 (17:28:13) and 1794129663 +0800 (17:21:03); %aI == %cI == epoch converted to +0800; author == committer; no date environment overrides."
    },
    {
      "id": "F3",
      "finding": "The 16:30/17:06 window is a prose estimate, not a clock",
      "evidence": "report.md line 8 and pipeline-status.json started_at/ended_at were hand-written. Machine evidence spans 16:41:40 (earliest probe captured_at) to 17:28:13 (final commit). The prose end time under-runs the real commit by about 22 minutes."
    },
    {
      "id": "F4",
      "finding": "captured_at values are runtime-generated, not back-filled",
      "evidence": "subtitle-signoff-tests.json captured_at 16:46:36+08:00 equals its own file mtime 16:46:36; signoff_before_after.json captured_at and mtime are both 16:46:36; other evidence files agree within seconds."
    },
    {
      "id": "F5",
      "finding": "Round-1 scripts hardcoded UTC+08:00 instead of reading host timezone",
      "evidence": "probe scripts used datetime.now(timezone(timedelta(hours=8))). The host IS UTC+08:00 with no DST, so recorded values are correct, but the implementation is a robustness defect. Round-2 evidence uses datetime.now().astimezone()."
    },
    {
      "id": "F6",
      "finding": "The 16:34 session clock is a DIFFERENT clock source, not a time reversal",
      "evidence": "It is the value quoted in the reviewer/session text. On this host, machine evidence in that period already existed at 16:41-16:46 (probe and test files). No file, commit or report was back-dated to match 16:34, and no future timestamp exists."
    }
  ],
  "conclusion": "There is NO system clock drift, NO forged time and NO back-filling. The apparent anomaly is fully explained by (a) a human-estimated 16:30-17:06 prose window that understates the real 17:21/17:28 commits, (b) a separate session/clock source quoting 16:34, and (c) hardcoded +08:00 in round-1 probe scripts. Historical reports are left untouched; this addendum is the only place the discrepancy is explained."
